        <bpmn:outgoing>W4067_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4067_Task4" name="OpEx/HR establish productivity baselines and targets (sales/labor-hour…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: OpEx/HR establish productivity baselines and targets (sales/labor-hour, units/labor-hour, cost-per-transaction) by function/site, aligned to staffing model (links to VS-19.3)
Responsible (R): OpEx / HR / Finance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4067_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4067_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4067_Task5" name="OpEx lead productivity improvement: standard work, scheduling optimization…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: OpEx lead productivity improvement: standard work, scheduling optimization, cross-training (links to VS-19/HR-022), automation (W4062), layout/tools
Responsible (R): OpEx / Site Leadership / HR
Accountable (A): Process Owners
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4067_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4067_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4067_Task6" name="OpEx/HR monitor productivity uplift, redeploy freed capacity to growth (not…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: OpEx/HR monitor productivity uplift, redeploy freed capacity to growth (not just cut), and ensure DOLE-compliant staffing (links to VS-84)
Responsible (R): OpEx / HR
Accountable (A): COO / CHRO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4067_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4067_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4067_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4067_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
